            "Pseudocontingency perceptions have been shown to reflect the skew in the marginals, independently of whether joint observations are actually presented, and according to Fiedler et al. (2007) a pseudocontingency perception arises when the distributions of two attributes in a group are skewed, so that skew in the same direction produces the appearance of a positive correlation and skew in opposite directions mimics a negative relationship.",
